/*  FUNCTION NAME:      FINDALL
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns a column of all non-sentinel answers from applying a predicate to each case. Predicate signature: LAMBDA(case, i) returning the answer, or the sentinel for no match.*/
/*  REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-02  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Make sentinel customisable (no_match) + add if_not_found return; accept horizontal or vertical cases
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Swap arg order: if_not_found before no_match (more commonly customised)
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Treat predicate errors as a miss instead of poisoning the whole result
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Add DEBUGGING help line calling out the 2-arg predicate gotcha
*/
FINDALL = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [cases],
    [predicate],
    [if_not_found],
    [no_match],
//  Help
    LET(Help, TEXTSPLIT(
                "FUNCTION:      →FINDALL(cases, predicate, [if_not_found], [no_match])¶" &
                "DESCRIPTION:   →Returns a column of all non-sentinel answers from applying predicate to each case.¶" &
                "VERSION:       →May 03 2026¶" &
                "PARAMETERS:    →¶" &
                "   cases          →(Required) Array of case tokens. Vertical or horizontal — flattened with TOCOL.¶" &
                "   predicate      →(Required) LAMBDA(case, i) returning the answer, or no_match for a miss. i is 1-based.¶" &
                "   if_not_found   →(Optional) Value to return when zero cases matched. Defaults to no_match.¶" &
                "   no_match       →(Optional) Sentinel value the predicate returns for no-match. Defaults to """". Override when """" is a valid answer.¶" &
                "EXAMPLE:       →¶" &
                "Formula        →=FINDALL({""a"";""b"";""c""}, LAMBDA(cur, i, IF(cur<>""b"", cur & i, """")))¶" &
                "Result         →{""a1""; ""c3""}¶" &
                "DEBUGGING:     →Predicate must take exactly two args — LAMBDA(case, i) — even if i is unused. A one-arg predicate silently returns no matches because every call errors and is caught as a miss. To diagnose, MAP the predicate over the cases yourself and look for #VALUE! in every row.¶" &
                "NOTE:          →Order of returned answers matches case order. The sentinel is compared with `<>` so it must be a comparable value (text, number, boolean) — not NA() or another error. Errors thrown inside the predicate are caught and treated as a miss.",
                "→", "¶"
                ),
    //  Check inputs
        Help?, ISOMITTED(cases),
    //  Procedure
        sentinel, IF(ISOMITTED(no_match), "", no_match),
        notFound, IF(ISOMITTED(if_not_found), sentinel, if_not_found),
        flat, TOCOL(cases),
        n, ROWS(flat),
        answers, MAP(flat, SEQUENCE(n), LAMBDA(cur, i, IFERROR(predicate(cur, i), sentinel))),
        result, IFERROR(FILTER(answers, answers <> sentinel, notFound), notFound),
        IF(Help?, Help, result)
)
);
